From: Project Luma
Subject: [PATCH] luma: windows appear once, fully inside a work area, after monitor changes

After resume or a dock change, windows were first painted where Mutter moved
them for the new layout, sometimes across two monitors that are not next to
each other, and window memory put them back only after the monitors had been
stable for 1.5 s. A monitor change that arrived before logind's wake signal
waited 30 s. A Wayland client that acknowledged an old configure late (Claude
after resume) could land with its top far above the panel, and that place
was then remembered.

Windows are now put back before the first frame of each new layout (after
the Shell updates its work areas) and confirmed when the monitors are
stable. A monitor change after resume is recognized by the monotonic clock
having stopped. A window moved for new monitors stays invisible until the
client shows it in place (at most 1 s). Any window left alone, or moved off
its work area by something other than the person, is brought fully inside
the work area of the monitor it overlaps most in one move. A place off the
work area is never remembered unless the person chose it.

